{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Some folks like the summertime [C7]when [F]they can stroll about
[G]Walking through the meadows green is [G7]pleasant no [C]doubt
But [C]just give me the wintertime [C7]when [F]snow is on the ground
For I [G7]found her when the snow was on the [C]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I traced her little footprints in the [G]snow, in the [G7]snow
[G7]Found her little footprints in the [C]snow, Lord
[C]I bless that happy day [C7]when [F]Nellie lost her way
For I [G]found her when the [G7]snow was on the [C]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I dropped in to see her there was a big round moon
Her mother said she just stepped out but would be returning soon
I found her little footprints and I traced them in the snow
I found her when the snow was on the ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Now she's up in heaven with the angel band
Someday I'm going to join her in that happy land
But every time the snow falls it brings back memories
For I found her when the snow was on the ground
{end_of_chorus}
